0..74 Comment "// Two data families of one shape are distinct types, equal only along the"
75..150 Comment "// path a stated equivalence makes between them. `Celsius` and `Fahrenheit`"
151..229 Comment "// each wrap an integer; the relabelling maps each constructor to the other\'s,"
230..308 Comment "// and transport along `ua` of that equivalence carries `Cel(20)` to `Fah(20)`"
309..387 Comment "// by a run: the HoTT book\'s § 2.10, Lemma 2.10.5, transport along `ua(e)` is"
388..465 Comment "// `e`. The twin, `pathological/data/nominal-distinctness.gandr`, refuses the"
466..522 Comment "// same value read as `Fahrenheit` with no path written."
